comments.body:
This rhymes with another issue we fixed a few weeks ago. I assume your config has `smooth_path: false` in your config file, yes? If you set it to `true`, can you reproduce? If not, then the solution is to do the following outside of the [if condition](https://github.com/ros-navigation/navigation2/blob/16acda895280e8b1e11db575d964bd717fb35b93/nav2_smac_planner/src/smac_planner_lattice.cpp#L233-L238) so it always runs to declare the parameters. That way if later toggled on/off the parameters are not being declared. This is a bug IMO in ros2 dynamic parameter callback design, but I understand the thinking. 

```
    SmootherParams params;
    params.get(node, name);
```

Let me know if that works. I can open PR(s) if you don't have time to

This is easy to solve 

@claude in the Smac Planner Hybrid A* and Smac Planner State Lattice, change in the `configure` method

```
  if (smooth_path) {
    SmootherParams params;
    params.get(node, name);
    _smoother = std::make_unique<Smoother>(params);
    _smoother->initialize(_metadata.min_turning_radius);
  }
```

to read

```
  SmootherParams params;
  params.get(node, name);
  if (smooth_path) {
    _smoother = std::make_unique<Smoother>(params);
    _smoother->initialize(_metadata.min_turning_radius);
  }
```

